{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["The reason for <b>And Cain said to Abel his brother</b> is that he entered with him into words of strife and quarrel in order to ambush him and kill him — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 4:8). And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 4:8) that he drew near to him and said to him all the reproofs with which HaShem had reproved him. In my opinion, it is connected with 'And it came to pass, while they were in the field,' for he said to him, 'Let us go out to the field,' and he killed him there in secret. And it is possible that his intent in the killing was that the world would be built from him, for he thought that his father would have no other seed. Furthermore, he also feared lest the foundation of the world's structure not come from his brother, whose offering had been accepted."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:29.355503052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}